My Conclusion: This distance is astronomically smaller than the particle’s own radius (10⁻⁶ m) and also far below any macroscopic length scale. In practical terms the dust grain will be completely reflected by the potential step; quantum‑mechanical penetration is essentially negligible.

Future Outlook: While the classical turning point is effectively at the surface of the step, a full quantum‑mechanical treatment (including tunnelling probabilities) could be explored for completeness. However, given the minuscule decay length, any tunnelling‐induced transmission would be vanishingly small, so for all realistic scenarios the particle behaves as if it were perfectly blocked by the step.

